			<div class="content" id="post-content-4478500">
									

<p>I think there should be the word &quot;The&quot; before the word &quot;entities&quot; in the middle of the 2nd paragraph of the Description. (You don't have to do this and I don't know if it was put there on purpose, that why I put &quot;I think&quot;) This is currently somewhere in my top 25 favorite Series-V SCPs.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;SPOILERS!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;close&nbsp;spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Aside from what I <em>think might</em> be a grammar or punctuation error, there is nothing else wrong with this SCP as far as I can tell. The document sounds scientific, there is a storyline that is shown through the Notes and Video Recordings. I like that Dr. Allegre appears to be &quot;friends&quot; or friendly towards SCP-4273 (Or at least that what I think) and then Dr. Allegre tries to cut SCP-4273 with garden shears and I shows betrayal which is something rare in SCP articles and when articles attempt to do betrayals, it usually doesn't do too well, but this article manages to perfectly pull of betrayal. Then I guess there a fight between Dr. Allegre and SCP-4273 and then Allegre possibly kills that SCP and it makes you think of what happened to both Dr. Allegre and SCP-4273. So yeah &#8230;I love your SCP</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>You got a +1 from me!</p>

