																		Junior Staff - Site Crit
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/malycegraves" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4916887); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4916887&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607200780" alt="MalyceGraves" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4916887)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/malycegraves" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4916887); return false;" >MalyceGraves</a></span> <span class="odate time_1579999047 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">26 Jan 2020 00:37</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4479369">
									

<p>Hello! I'm <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/malycegraves" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4916887); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4916887&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1579999124" alt="MalyceGraves" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4916887)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/malycegraves" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4916887); return false;">MalyceGraves</a></span> and I'll be performing a site crit review of this piece today.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<h3><span>Overall</span></h3>
<p>I think that some of the problems that you're running into here is that it's simply not that interesting. The bulk of the writing isn't bad, just it's a story that doesn't really go anywhere. The narrative arc of a group of trees that become more aggressive is&#8230; meh.</p>
<p>I think that you have ground here to build a more complete narrative, but as it stands this is simply a thing what does a thing with a few more steps.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4273 entities demonstrate a competent level of mimicry when observing human behaviour.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I saw this and I was expecting more of this. I was disappointed when I didn't really see anything that really speaks to this. Maybe a bit when the neutralized instance shrank in fear, but that was about it.</p>
<hr />
<h3><span>SPaG</span></h3>
<p>It's clear that you've gone over this a bunch and fixed any gross errors. That's a good thing.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>in the presence of Dr.Allegre since the second week of January.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Missing a space after Dr.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>These changes are often accompanied by the restructuring of the trunk, repositioning of branches and growth of additional roots.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Oxford comma. Also, re-positioning.</p>
<hr />
<h3><span>Consistency/Flow</span></h3>
<blockquote>
<p>They will not engage in activities that they perceive to be harmful to their well being or other plant life.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Consider: They will not engage in activities that they perceive to be harmful to themselves, or to the well-being of other forms of plant life. This indicates an awareness of themselves as part of a greater ecosystem, and may connote the existence of feelings of camaraderie.</p>
<p>I suggest the addition as a way to greater showcase their sentience/potential sapience. Self awareness plays a role in that, and I think drawing attention to it adds a bit more to our willingness to &quot;feel&quot; for the plight of what is otherwise a decorative plant.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Pejorative language directed toward the entities will also elicit a negative response.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Is this a tone thing, or actual understanding of the language being spoken? Many domesticated animals have shown that they are more aware of the tone than of the actual words.</p>
<p>I assume that the instances were forcibly separated between the first video log and the second. There is no link between the two, so it appears as if they're all present, then suddenly there's only one. I think this could be fixed by adding something in the &quot;Notes:&quot; section.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>1437: SCP-4273-1 grows several additional branches and attaches them to Dr. Allegre's arm.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>How do they &quot;attach&quot;? I think the better phrasing would be &quot;&#8230;and clutches at Dr. Allegre's arm.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Dr. Allegre switches on the television present within the cell and tunes into [REDACTED],</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why did you redact that? You could say that it is a live feed, pre-recorded news footage, etc.</p>
<p>Also, modern televisions don't have switches anymore, so I think the more accurate phrasing here would be &quot;Dr. Allegre activates the television&#8230;&quot; or a video display monitor. &quot;switching on a television&quot; seems incredibly archaic in this context.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><em>&#8230;that could prove sapience if we test further. I'll ask the site manager for a pair of shears.</em></p>
<p><em>~Melissa</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p>I assume this is Dr. Allegre. I also recognize that this is her personal note, but in this context, I believe that signing it Dr. Allegre is more appropriate.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Entity reconstructs itself into [REDACTED] times its original height.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This seems pointlessly redacted.</p>
<hr />
<h3><span>Closing Remarks</span></h3>
<p>I think that one of the things here that I should point out is that &quot;bonsai&quot; is not referencing a specific type of plant, but rather the practice of producing an end result. I think that that is grounds for very fertile storytelling, and should be utilized.</p>
<p>Example, do the different trees behave differently depending on their original species? Maybe the reason they're so unfriendly towards being sheared is due to some past trauma? Do they have any similarities to the large trees they are supposed to represent? Is there any additional iconography within their tray/pot/whatever?</p>
<p>Furthermore, I think you could explore more about where they came from, how the Foundation got a hold of them. Did they just appear in containment one day? Did someone drop them off? Were they acquired in an estate sale?</p>
<p>Like I said before. The skip isn't poorly written from a technical standpoint, but it leaves a lot out that I don't think that it being streamlined and short is best served by.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I hope that this helps you, not only with this piece, but your future pieces as well.</p>
