				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/the-trixter" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3116978); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3116978&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607200781" alt="The Trixter" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3116978)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/the-trixter" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3116978); return false;" >The Trixter</a></span> <span class="odate time_1585380323 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">28 Mar 2020 07:25</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4568570">
									

<p>I have two main problems with this skip,</p>
<ol>
<li>The Writing</li>
<li>The Appeal</li>
</ol>
<p>First, the writing. It feels very stilted and rather rough. None of the sentences flow together well to create a good reading experience. Writing out the skip with sentence structure in mind would have helped here. Near the end of the skip you write about one of the SCP-4273 instances being contained in a pot in the <em>very last</em> recording.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Dr. Allegre manages to knock SCP-4273-1's pot onto the ground, shattering it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is not mentioned in <em>any</em> other part of the text. This sounds like something that would be important to include in the Special Containment Procedures. Speaking of Containment Procedures, I know that short Special Containment Procedures are normally a nitpick, but this is a bit too little.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>All SCP-4273 entities are to be contained within a standard botanical containment cell. Each entity is to remain isolated outside of testing purposes.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>There should be more than two short sentences that barely tell us anything. Don't ignore them, they're there for a reason. There's also other instances of you including things that should be in the containment procedures in other parts of the article.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Dr. Allegre enters SCP-4273-2's containment cell and proceeds to water the entity with the provided pail.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Do the SCP-4273 instances require water? Do they require sunlight? All these questions were most likely not thought of in the rush to get the &quot;exiting&quot; details into the story. Think through the basics of your skip before you go for the interesting stuff. There also seems to be a moderate amount of grammatical errors throughout your story, this can be solved with a peer review (preferably 2).</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The other SCP-4273 entities grow several dozen branches as their leaves change into a brilliant shade of red.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>Skips aren't Novels</strong> nobody wishing to know about your scp cares about how much imagery is included. Ditch the fancy stuff and get straight to the point if you can.<br />
Secondly, the appeal. What I mean by this is what makes your skip actually interesting. Personally, I find this work to be rather dull. There's nothing that really make's it interesting. There's nothing interesting in the recordings (Why should I care if they're sapient or not). Your special containment procedures are at best poorly thought out and at worst lazy. The overall plot of these plant's being sentient doesn't interest me at all because I've seen this <em>a thousand times over</em> better executed. Overall, your skip is poorly constructed and poorly thought out.</p>
<p>This skip mainly needs more planning out and peer editing. It always helps to have a second set of eyes to look over your work.</p>
<p>Those are my thoughts. Thanks for reading.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
